//RS //! This test fails the build on a second copy. It looks for two things:
//RS //!   1. a function that takes a float sequence and carries a statistics name
//RS //!      (`sum`, `mean`, `variance`, …) outside the kernel;
//RS //!   2. the kernel's own arithmetic fingerprints — the Neumaier compensation
//RS //!      step and the Welford update — outside the kernel.
